Just to add something: Rodney on his own isn't too bad. Rodney, doubled, 
is still fightable provided you do it from a doorway or similar 
position. Rodney, doubled, plus the high priest, is trouble incarnate.

If you find out that Rodney's going for the amulet when you get to 
Sanctum, leave him alone and concentrate on taking out the masses of 
cannon-fodder. Search for the Inner Sanctum door, but leave it shut and 
let him fight the high priest. Do not on any account allow yourself to 
be surrounded by all 3. (I made the mistake of doing that last game, and 
didn't live to regret it.)

Alternatively you can /oDeath Rodney, then fight the high priest on your 
own (word is he's immune to /oDeath). Or bring a rubber chicken. It's 
best, when fighting this gang, not to rely upon your raw combat skill to 
carry the day. For style points I guess you could reverse-geno black 
dragons, or apply a cursed figurine of one, and then try to carom a 
disintegration blast off yourself... but that's nearly as tricky as 
meleeing them.

Has anyone tried this method:
- get disint-resist,
- pick up one of the priests' corpses,
- enter the Inner Sanctum,
- then sac it on Moloch's altar?

Could you kill Rodney and the high priest with the wide-angle D-beam 
that way?

YANI - if Rodney is doubled, when one of his doubles gets stoned, the 
other should immediately cast STF on him...

And bring lots of HW to rebless items after you RC them. Moloch's 
priests can curse items, which is a major PITA. Carrying more than a few 
RCs would help too.

